# Design system

Never hard-code `Color(0x…)`, `Colors.*`, raw padding numbers, or user-facing strings.

```dart
// ✅
final colors = context.appPalette;
padding: const EdgeInsets.all(AppSpacing.md),
style: AppTextStyles.body1(colors),
Text(LocaleKeys.homeTitle.tr),
Icon(Icons.home, size: AppIconSize.md, color: colors.primary),

// ❌ Color(0xFF2D6A4F), EdgeInsets.all(13), Text('Hello'), CupertinoIcons
```

- Colors live only in `AppColors.light` / `AppColors.dark`.
- Gradients: `AppGradients.primary` / `primaryHero` / `accent` from palette tokens.
- Spacing: `AppSpacing`. Radius: `AppRadius` (lg 24, xl 32). Type: Cairo via `AppTextStyles`.
- Main chrome: `AppFloatingNavBar` + `AppNavFab` (notched floating bar, primary blue FAB).
- Home top: theme/locale as icon buttons only. Name prompt is one field, then a welcome banner.
- New token → add to core theme first, then use it.
- New copy → `LocaleKeys` + `en_us.dart` + `ar_sa.dart`.
- Reuse `lib/shared/widgets` (`AppButton`, `AppCard`, `AppScaffold`). Do not rebuild them in a page.
